blocks.text:
Big progress:
- Full suite: 5603 passed, 0 failed (5594 + 9 new) ✓
- Regressions FIXED: matchesGuards 18.1 → 16 (improved), queryPrs 28 → 26 (improved) ✓
- But TWO new offenders:
 - `_labeledEventFor: 9` — my helper has CC 9?! I estimated 8. The actual counting: 1 + if(!ev||) 2 + ternary 2 + if 1 + (&&) 1 + (||) 1 = 8... measured 9. One more operator than I counted — `(ev.actor && ev.actor.login) || null` is && and || = 2, plus `ev.created_at || null` = +1 → total: 1+2+2+1+2+1 = 9 ✓ my miscount.
 - `transplantSequence: 10` — I estimated 8; actual 10. Recount: 1 + `input.source||{}` 1 + `source.labels||[]` 1 + `input.base||{...}` 1 + if(skip) 1 + if(refusal) 1 + `marker = input.marker || null` 1 + if(parked) 1 + if(!shaInfo) 1 + if(orphan) 1 = 10 ✓ (I forgot the `|| null` on marker).

Wait — but the coverage: `_labeledEventFor` at 100% → CRAP 9 > 8 fails. transplantSequence CC 10 at 100% → 10.

Interesting: the earlier run had `parseTransplantMarker 12 95.2%` etc. — now all those pass (≤8). Also `guestPrBody` passes now (test coverage raised it to 100% → CRAP 8.0 ✓ — confirming 8.0 passes the gate).

Fix the two remaining:
1. `_labeledEventFor` CC 9 → split further: move the login/createdAt extraction into the returned object differently:
``
function _eventActorLogin(ev) {
   return (ev.actor && ev.actor.login) || null;  // CC 3
}
function _labeledEventFor(ev, labelName) {
   if (!ev || ev.event !== 'labeled') return null;     // +2
   var name = (ev.label && typeof ev.label === 'object') ? ev.label.name : ev.label; // +2
   if (String(name) !== String(labelName)) return null; // +1
   return { login: _eventActorLogin(ev), createdAt: ev.created_at || null }; // +1
}
``
CC = 1+2+2+1+1 = 7 ✓. `_eventActorLogin` CC 3 ✓ covered.

2. `transplantSequence` CC 10 → shave 2. Options:
  - `var marker = input.marker || null;` → drop the `|| null` (pass input.marker directly; all consumers handle undefined falsy: `marker && marker.state`, `resolveTransplantSha(marker, ...)` reads `marker && marker.head`, `!marker`) → −1 → 9.
  - `var base = input.base || { owner: '', repo: '', baseBranch: cfg.baseBranch };` — this default matters: tests may call without base? baseInput always has base... but the module contract allows missing base (baseBranch fallback to cfg.baseBranch). Moving the resolution into the helpers that need it: only `_transplantRefuseDecision` (base.owner/base.repo) and `transplantBodySteps` callers (park-reset + fresh + orphan pass base through) use it. Alternative: resolve base ONCE but without the `||`: `var base = input.base;` then `_transplantRefuseDecision` handles missing base? isCrossRepoHead(headRepo, base.owner...) — base.owner on undefined → crash. Keep the fallback somewhere. Hmm.
  - Move the no-ref park branch into a helper: `_noRefParkDecision(input, cfg, source, marker, audit)`? The shaInfo check stays... The `if (!shaInfo) return park` — I can fold sha resolution INTO `_orphanDecision`-style helper: create `_shaOrPark(input, cfg, source, marker, audit)` returning either {shaInfo} or a park decision:

``
